From b2316fe6356cb02152f0dd0c2097f7ebab88cc55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kotoriqaq0 <2216804318@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 21:42:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add knorm KV cache compression module

New module vllm/knorm/: KnormConfig (env-based configuration),
attention wrapper (key L2 norm computation on CUDA/Ascend),
KnormFullAttentionManager (KV cache block eviction based on
compression ratio), and runtime hooks (score collection and
routing between model runner and scheduler).

Integration into v1 core: scheduler routes block scores from
ModelRunnerOutput to KV cache manager; single_type_kv_cache_manager
registers KnormFullAttentionManager as default for FullAttentionSpec;
gpu_model_runner installs attention wrapper and collects norms
after each model forward.

Knorm (Devoto et al., 2024) shows that KV cache blocks with high
key L2 norms receive low attention scores during decoding, making
them safe to evict. This module reduces KV cache memory usage with
minimal quality loss, controlled via environment variables.

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: kotoriqaq0 <2216804318@qq.com>
